keholders, responding to inquiries, processing requests, and facilitating communication with the AVP;  Monitor the AVP's email account, distributing messages as needed and coordinating responses on behalf of the Office;  Review incoming materials and requests, including confidential matters, and note information requiring follow-up;  Coordinate and process requests requiring the AVP's review, approval, or signature;  Maintain records, filing systems, tracking tools, and databases in accordance with university policies, privacy requirements, and confidentiality standards;  Act as a liaison between Alumni & Development, Advancement units, and other University departments to facilitate effective communication and administrative support;  Maintain positive, collaborative relationships with campus and external partners, including volunteers, alumni and donors, to ensure excellent customer service;  Liaise with other Alumni and Development leadership offices and University departments as needed regarding Alumni & Development activities to ensure awareness and appropriate coordination;  Administer and prioritize the AVP's schedule, coordinating meetings and engagement opportunities while balancing competing priorities;  Schedule and coordinate meetings for the AVP and leadership team, including aligning participant schedules, arranging logistics, and ensuring necessary preparation requirements are addressed;  Prepare and assemble briefing materials, reports, correspondence, and supporting documentation for meetings and stakeholder engagements;  Maintain the accuracy and integrity of database records through data entry, updates, tracking, and reporting activities in accordance with privacy requirements;    Key Skills and Experience:   College Diploma in related discipline or the equivalent combination of education and experience.  Knowledge of office administration concepts, practices and techniques;  Knowledge of the administrative functions and governance structures withi